3962130802514507532,Db8UPj9grcM,https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db8UPj9grcM/,reel,2026-08-12T13:55:13.000Z,229206,4574,17939501301311891,"A Matter of Shame Nearly 80 years after Independence, it is deeply disappointing that a historic and culturally significant city like Prayagraj continues to struggle with basic electricity issues. What is even more frustrating is that law-abiding consumers who pay their electricity bills honestly and on time are repeatedly subjected to inspections and enquiries, while the real problem of illegal connections and electricity theft often remains inadequately addressed. Thousands of ordinary people depend on legitimate businesses for their livelihoods. We invest, pay taxes and electricity bills, create employment and contribute to the local economy. Yet, instead of being encouraged, honest consumers are often made to feel like offenders. If electricity theft is taking place, the authorities must identify the actual offenders and take strict action against them. There must be transparency, accountability and equal enforcement of the law. A system that questions honest consumers while failing to effectively control power theft is not only inefficient—it is deeply unfair. Prayagraj deserves reliable electricity, responsible administration and a system where the honest citizen is protected, not penalised. This is not merely an electricity issue; it is an issue of governance, accountability and public trust.",2026-08-13T18:32:42.000Z,1,0,,0,amanfit_run,Aman Agarwal,7101272861,false,https://www.instagram.com/amanfit_run/
