3963510110499812330,DcBN3IoArPq,https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcBN3IoArPq/,reel,2026-08-14T11:36:01.000Z,212579,8816,18088297331543357,"🕉️🔱⚛️🔬 Scientists & Technologists Inspired by Sanatana Dharma / Hinduism 1. Erwin Schrödinger — Nobel Prize, Physics — Inspired by the Upanishads/Vedanta; emphasized the unity of consciousness. 2. J. Robert Oppenheimer — Physicist, Manhattan Project Director — Studied Sanskrit and the Bhagavad Gita, which deeply influenced his thinking. 3. Werner Heisenberg — Nobel Prize, Physics — Engaged with Indian philosophy and Vedanta while reflecting on quantum theory. 4. Niels Bohr — Nobel Prize, Physics — Interested in Upanishadic thought and Eastern philosophical ideas. 5. Nikola Tesla — Inventor & Electrical Engineer — Engaged with Swami Vivekananda and concepts of Prana and Akasha. 6. David Bohm — Quantum Physicist — Explored wholeness, consciousness and interconnectedness in dialogue with Indian thought. 7. Wolfgang Pauli — Nobel Prize, Physics — Explored consciousness, symbolism and Eastern philosophy. 8. Carl Sagan — Astronomer & Cosmologist — Appreciated Hindu concepts of cyclic cosmic time and vast cosmic ages. 9. Fritjof Capra — Physicist & Systems Theorist — Compared modern physics with Vedanta and Eastern philosophies. 10. George Sudarshan — Theoretical Physicist — Major quantum physicist with a strong interest in Vedanta and Indian philosophy. 11. Srinivasa Ramanujan — Mathematician, Fellow of the Royal Society — Devout Hindu; said mathematical insights came through Goddess Namagiri’s blessing. His major work included number theory, infinite series, continued fractions and partition theory. 12. Jagadish Chandra Bose — Physicist & Biologist — Practised science within a strong Indian intellectual and cultural tradition. 13. Satyendra Nath Bose — Physicist, Padma Vibhushan — Pioneer of quantum statistics; part of India's classical intellectual tradition. 14. Vikram Sarabhai — Physicist, ISRO Founder — Connected India's scientific advancement with its civilizational heritage. 15. C. V. Raman — Nobel Prize, Physics — A spiritually inclined Hindu who valued India's Sanatana Dharma heritage and its intellectual traditions, while championing scientific inquiry.",2026-08-14T18:09:53.000Z,0,0,,0,spidey_0733,Spidey,71401116939,false,https://www.instagram.com/spidey_0733/
